; docs/semantics/kinds/defadapter.eadl — the kind the engine's adapter catalog is written with.
;
; ROADMAP.md §5.4: "Engine search may realize an OS feature indirectly from lower-level hardware functionality. A
; software deadline service can use a supported relative timer through an engine-owned adapter". The design record
; `docs/specs/adapters/decision_engine-adapters.md` §1 decides that each adapter the engine knows is one `defadapter`
; entry of `docs/semantics/adapters/adapters.eadl`: what it requires of the one provider it programs, what it offers
; over it, the level its code runs at, and what it owes.
;
; ⭐ DECLARED WITH `defkind`, LIKE `deffact`. It carries no behaviour (reference §7 rule 3): its clauses hold names,
; forms and one line of text. What an instance's offers are, and how the search binds one, is engine knowledge in
; `crates/eadl-resolve` (`adapter.rs`, `search.rs`); the configuration checker holds its own table of the same kinds,
; `crates/archogen-plan-check/src/adapters.rs`, held equal to this file's reading by a derivation test.
;
; ⛔ NO DESCRIPTION'S REGISTRY HOLDS THIS KIND. A description writes no adapter, imports none and names none (record
; §1.1). Any file that writes one is the language's own definition and not a description, and `archogen check`
; answers it as it answers a kind module, exit `20`.
;
; THE CLAUSES, as the record's §1.3 states them:
;
;   doc          what the adapter does, one line; required
;   beneath      what it requires of the one provider it programs: `needs` lists and constraints, a side the
;                relation reads as any requirer's
;   offers       what an instance offers, each fact once: `(f v)`, a value; `(f (from g))`, the provider's own value
;                of `g`, a fact of `f`'s domain; or `(f (obliged))`, a bound the instance takes on at its requester's
;                tightest bound on `f`
;   level        the level of `reachable-at-privilege`'s domain its code runs at, model §8 rule 9's
;   obligations  what the realization owes, each `(obligation NAME (doc "…"))`
;   costs        the interrupts its code takes, each `(interrupt NAME (doc "…"))`, for the analysis to charge
;   mediates     `true` for a kind that crosses a mediation boundary, offered only where a requirer allows mediation;
;                absent meaning `false`

(eadl-version eadl/1)

(defkind defadapter
  (doc "an adapter the engine supplies: what it requires of the provider it programs, what it offers over it, and what it owes")
  (name required)
  (clause doc (cardinality one) (holds values string))
  (clause beneath (cardinality one) (holds forms))
  (clause offers (cardinality one) (holds forms))
  (clause level (cardinality one) (holds values symbol))
  (clause obligations (cardinality at-most-one) (holds forms))
  (clause costs (cardinality at-most-one) (holds forms))
  (clause mediates (cardinality at-most-one) (holds values symbol)))
